---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BROKER, FOOTER_LINE, DISCLAIMER_LONG } from '../config/site';

const paragraphs = DISCLAIMER_LONG.split('\n\n');
---

<Base
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="Terms on which information on thepreconmarket.ca is provided. General information about published program rules, not tax, legal or accounting advice."
  kicker={['Ontario', 'Disclaimer']}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Disclaimer', href: '/disclaimer' }]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[720px] px-4 pt-8 sm:px-6">
    <p class="section-label">Disclaimer</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-[1.85rem] font-semibold sm:text-[2.2rem]">Terms of information</h1>

    <div class="prose-precon mt-8">
      {paragraphs.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}

      <h2>About the figures on this site</h2>
      <p>
        Dollar amounts shown anywhere on this site, including in the rebate checker, are
        <strong> maximums for illustration</strong>. They are produced from published program
        thresholds and are expressed as "up to" amounts deliberately. Your actual entitlement
        depends on your circumstances, the wording of your agreement of purchase and sale, and
        program rules that may change.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where published guidance does not state an amount clearly enough for us to model it, the
        checker shows a flag rather than a number. A figure we are not confident in would be worse
        than no figure, because you would plan around it.
      </p>

      <h2>About sources</h2>
      <p>
        Pages that make claims about tax or contract rules cite their sources, and those citations
        link to the originals, Canada Revenue Agency notices, Ontario government pages, Tarion's
        coverage terms, and the Condominium Authority of Ontario. Where sources disagree, or where
        the position is genuinely unsettled, the page says so rather than picking the more
        flattering answer.
      </p>
      <p>
        Program rules change. Each page carries a revision date. If you are reading this long after
        that date, verify the current position before relying on it.
      </p>

      <h2>About third-party information</h2>
      <p>
        Project details, pricing, sizes, deposit structures, occupancy dates, incentives, come
        from builder and industry sources and are subject to change without notice. They are
        provided for general information and are not an offer or a representation. Confirm all
        details directly with the builder before making any decision.
      </p>

      <h2>Professional registration</h2>
      <p>{FOOTER_LINE}</p>
      <p>
        {BROKER.name} is a licensed real estate Broker registered with the Real Estate Council of
        Ontario, operating under {BROKER.brokerage}. He is not a lawyer, accountant or mortgage
        agent.
      </p>
      <p>
        Not intended to solicit buyers or sellers currently under contract with another brokerage.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
